  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough next Wednesday\n\nA strong 700 mb jet of 50-60 kts will be moving across Southeast \nMontana throughout the day today. The jet will be strongest in the\nmorning hours over eastern parts of the forecast area. A strong\neast/west pressure gradient will set up behind the cold front \nhelping to enhance strong winds. Given that wind gusts have \nremained below warning levels (60 mph) this evening in the west, \nand the strongest 700 mb winds are expected to occur before the \nbest lapse rates Wednesday, winds gusts are expected to remain in \nthe 40-55 mph range. Even though the strongest winds are expected \nearlier in the day, most of Southeast Montana can expect winds \ngusting in the 30s mph for most of the day. \n\nTemperatures will be near to slightly below average in the 60s and\n70s F Wednesday and Thursday under northwest flow. Upper level\ntroughing moves to the east Friday bringing warmer temperatures in\nthe 70s and 80s F. The weather is expected to get more active\nSaturday through Monday as an upper level waves moves from the\nPacific Coast through southern Canada. Another shortwave further\nsouth is expected to create low pressure over the central plains\nallowing southerly winds to advect anomalously high moisture\nvalues into Montana. Even though this pattern appears to be\nfavorable for convection, forecast soundings currently show \ncapping limiting convective potential. While convective potential\nis still highly uncertain, 40-70% precipitation chances are\npresent over the weekend. The NBM is giving locations east of\nBillings a 30-70% chance of getting greater than 0.25 inches of\nprecipitation over the weekend. Persistent temperatures in the \n70s and 80s F are expected Saturday through early next week. \nTorgerson",
